From e13dce3d5d18ccd37990320529e143db3372b291 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:41:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/28] Drone: steady pads, isochronic attack/release,
 triplets, knob sections, reverb send; LFO start fix

Drone (mastertune-v13):
- The pads no longer pulse with the beat (tiring to look at).
- Isochronic pulses have an attack and a release per tone (0-50, 2 % steps of the half cycle the pulse is on,
  never shorter than 1 ms); 6 matches v12's fixed edges at a 10 Hz beat.
- Tempo sync also in triplets: 1/1T to 1/64T, locked to the triplet grid.
- The gold knobs follow the mod buttons: Level/Pan, Cutoff/Res = pitch/beat (as before), Attack/Release = the
  pulse, Sidechain/Reverb = the whole drone's ducking and its new reverb send; LEDs and knob indicators show it.
- A send to the song's reverb (0-50), gliding per sample; without it the drone mixes in as in v12.
- Saved with the song; older firmware ignores the new attributes.

Fix (1.2.1): LFO phase and hold value, and a Sound's skip-rendering timestamps, were uninitialised, so LFOs and
mod FX started at a random phase on each load and a random-walk LFO could start far out of range.

